# Local test settings. Copy to .env, which is never committed.
#
#   cp env.example .env
#
# Everything here is optional. With no .env the test suite runs exactly as it
# does in CI: against a mock device, with an obviously fake serial.
#
# The point of this file is that a real handset can be named for local runs
# without a device identifier ever being written into the repository. This one
# is public, and a serial identifies a specific phone.

# The serial the fixtures use in place of the fake one. `adb devices` prints it.
# ANDROID_RESCUE_TEST_SERIAL=

# A display name for that handset, used only in test output.
# ANDROID_RESCUE_TEST_MODEL=

# Set to 1 to run tests/test_real_device.sh against a phone on USB. Unset, it
# skips and the suite passes on a machine with no device, which is how CI runs.
#
# With it set, ANDROID_RESCUE_TEST_SERIAL is required and becomes ANDROID_SERIAL
# for the run, so every adb call targets that handset. Without that, adb refuses
# outright when two phones are attached, or talks to the wrong one when the
# phone you meant is not the only one plugged in.
#
# The device test is read-only: it probes and reads state. It copies nothing off
# the phone and writes nothing to it.
# ANDROID_RESCUE_TEST_DEVICE=
